<newsitem itemid="406972" id="root" date="1997-02-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LeisureNet lifts year shr, div.</title>
<headline>LeisureNet lifts year shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)     26.90	vs   21.10</p>
<p>    Yr div (cts)		7.40	vs    5.90</p>
<p>    Net profit		 31.76	vs   17.44</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    49.31	vs   28.37</p>
<p>    Tax			  17.55	vs   10.93</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    10.92	vs    6.46</p>
<p>    Turnover		  322.28	vs  178.59</p>
<p>Div payable April 16</p>
<p>on register March 14</p>
<p>Full name: LeisureNet Ltd (health, leisure, food and education operations)</p>
<p>Share of associates'</p>
<p>    income			1.17	vs    -</p>
<p>    Exceptional item	   -	  vs    1.08</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said all divisions were expected to show continued growth.</p>
<p>Shareholders will be given the option to receive capitalisation shares in lieu of the dividend. Deatails will be posted on March 20.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
